ARGBToUVMatrixRow_SVE2's tail loop stores with the all-true p0, so each pass
writes VL/64 bytes of U and of V whatever is left of the row. That is exact
at VL=128 and a heap overflow past it (256-bit SVE: Graviton3, or qemu's
default 512): libavif's 4x4 RGBA->I420 test trips musl's free(). Store with
p1, the width predicate the loads already use (one U/V byte per pixel pair).
Upstream rewrote the kernel in 3d66e94 (2025-03), after the 1908 nixpkgs
ships.

--- a/source/row_sve.cc
+++ b/source/row_sve.cc
@@ -386,8 +386,8 @@
       "addhnb   z16.b, z16.h, z26.h                 \n"  // U
       "addhnb   z20.b, z20.h, z26.h                 \n"  // V
 
-      "st1b     {z16.d}, p0, [%[dst_u]]             \n"  // U
-      "st1b     {z20.d}, p0, [%[dst_v]]             \n"  // V
+      "st1b     {z16.d}, p1, [%[dst_u]]             \n"  // U
+      "st1b     {z20.d}, p1, [%[dst_v]]             \n"  // V
       "incd     %[dst_u]                            \n"
       "incd     %[dst_v]                            \n"
       "b.gt     3b                                  \n"
